  "body": "I'm trying to make all the inputs to the navigation algorithm explicit. I think this is the comprehensive list:\r\n\r\n- _resource_\r\n- [source browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#source-browsing-context) (see #1130)\r\n- navigation type (\"form-submission\" or \"other\")\r\n- [_exceptionsEnabled_](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#exceptions-enabled)\r\n- [_replacementEnabled_](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#navigation-replacement-enabled)\r\n- [reload-triggered navigation](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#reload-triggered-navigation)\r\n- [entry update](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#entry-update)\r\n\r\nI'd like to focus here on reload-triggered, entry update, and replacement enabled, as I think they can be consolidated. In particular, looking at the call sites:\r\n\r\n- `location.reload()` and user-triggered reloads set reload-triggered = true, entry update = true, replacement enabled = false\r\n- History traversal with no bfcache entry ([traverse the history](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#traverse-the-history) step 1) sets reload-triggered = false, entry update = true, replacement enabled = false\r\n- A bunch of places use _replacementEnabled_, but never in combination with the other two.\r\n\r\nSo I think we should convert these three into a new parameter, call it _historyHandling_, with the following values. Here I use (x, y, z) to represent the values of (reload-triggered, entry update, replacement enabled).\r\n\r\n- \"`default`\": equivalent to (false, false, false)\r\n- \"`reload`\": equivalent to (true, true, false)\r\n- \"`entry update`\": equivalent to (false, true, false)\r\n- \"`replace`\": equivalent to (false, false, true)\r\n\r\nThis seems like a big improvement, since it makes it clear there are only 4 valid states, not 2<sup>3</sup> = 8.\r\n\r\nAny bikeshedding on these names is welcome. Example ideas:\r\n\r\n- \"reload entry update\" instead of just \"reload\"\r\n- \"repopulate bfcache\" instead of \"entry update\"",
